So I was playing a female eleven ranger (cha) on a public server for
the second time today, and was able to enter the Mines before I was
really hassled. I fell through two trapdoors one just right after
another, and was cut off from all of the arrows still littering the
ground. I still had about 50 mixed arrows left, so I set off to find
the up staircase, flaunting my +4 (very rotted) elven cloak. I was able
to clear out most of the level, and killed two leprechauns, the last of
whom left a corpse. I ate it for the nutritional value, and
unfortunately contracted a bad case of teleportitis.

It took me about an hour to wander around this level and pick up all of
my arrows, as I kept on teleporting to the other side of the
dungeon............ By this time I was sufficiently bored to not bother
to pick up my arrows two dungeon levels up, and went down to the next
level. I got maybe half-way, encountering another leprechaun, a stone
giant, and some owlbears, before I had something blow up in my face and
give me hallucinations. That wouldn't be so bad if I didn't fall
through yet another trap door a few steps later.

Immediately, something came up and attacked. I shot 5 arrows at it, and
finished it off. The corpse told me that it was a large housecat named
Rex. Good, I thought - someone's left a bone here. I went out the door
of the small room that I was in and bumped into something. That
something wielded his silver sabre and began to attack. The blowing of
the whistle called in the rest of the Minetown guard, and I thought I
was finished. Fortunately, my single wand was a wand of sleep, which
got the guard captain sucking his thumb. My expert ranking at bow and
my few remaining arrows were sufficient to finish of the entire guard
and a monkey, miraculously, and by this time the hallucinations wore
off.

I wandered around and killed a few rogue things, including a drunk
incubus, when I found this guy's bone file at the door of the temple. I
killed his ghost eventually, having to switch between my few remaining
arrows and pick them up a few times, and set out to determine the b/u/c
of his items. I considered converting the alter to chaotic, but as my
last 2 out of 6 deaths as a ran-fem-elv-cha came from trying to wrench
minetown altars from venus, I decided to save that task for later, and
use the fountains for decursing instead of holy water. I made a few
stacks of items, and eventually had a bag of holding (albeit cursed), a
silver sabre, a magic marker (I later found out that it was 0:98), 3
learned spells that I could successfully cast, and several other good
items.

Teleportitis eventually flung me out of the temple, and so I went to
explore the side rooms, finding yet another bone file of someone who
died to a woodland elf. Fortunately, this elf was peaceful to his
brethern, so I looted this guy's (not quite as good) stuff, and walked
back to the altar with his ghost trailing me, as I hadn't enough arrows
to finish it off, and the autoquiver had loaded my starting dagger into
my bow several times already. I got the b/u/c of these new items sorted
out, and was about to uncurse some of the first guy's better items when
a few jackals came up. I shot my ragtag arrows at them, and walked over
to pick them up, when the second guy's ghost came over. Not a problem,
I thought, and pulled out my silver sabre, which did no damage. Putting
that away, I was going to ignore it when a barrow-wight pulled up.

I got 5 arrows and my dagger together, and retreated into a small room,
holding the doorway. I threw all of my ammo at it, and got no results.
I drank a full healing pot after it got me down to 15 hp, and I was
desperate enough to shoot my wands. I had 5 of them, including my
trusty wand of sleep. So I shot a bolt from it at the wight, doing
nothing, and it bounced. Thankfully, I had resistance to sleep, so I
was able to try the next wand. All it managed to do was carve out a
straight line in the walls of the opposite room, and I also had a
duplicate of it, so there were 2 wands left. The next one had no
effect, so I used the last one, which just happened to be a wand of
magic missile.

One hit vanquished the wight, and another felled the ghost.
Teleportitis threw me somewhere else, but I strolled back, victorious,
and dipped a cursed tattered cape into a fountain. First time, nothing.
Second time, nothing. Third time, nothing. Fourth time, a water demon
came. I #chatted to it in hopes of a wish, but all it did was attack
me. For some reason, I saw two &'s, of different colours, so I ; 'd the
one below me, showing &: a major demon (Yeenoghu). So I contemplated my
options, and chose to pray, when I found out that I had pressed the
down command (which I had used for the examine tool) again.

You begin bashing monsters with your bow.
Yeenoghu hits!
Yeenoghu hurls a flask of white liquid at you!
You have a terrible headache!
Yeenoghu hits! Yeenoghu hits! Yeenoghu hits! Yeenoghu hits!
You die....
